{"name":"Citron Goby","hex":"#deff00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"citron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small citrus tree, Citrus medica.\nThe fruit of a citron tree.\n\nThe candied rind of the citron fruit.\nA greenish yellow colour, inspired by the color of the rind of the citron fruit.","The fruit of a citron tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish yellow colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citron"},{"term":"goby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small fish from the large family Gobiidae, in which the pelvic fins are fused to form a disc-shaped sucker.","A gudgeon, a fish of the subfamily Gobioninae, such as a common gudgeon (Gobio gobio)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citron","blocks":[{"text":"The citron is a large fragrant citrus fruit with a thick, coarse rind. It resembles a lemon, but is larger. It is one of the original citrus fruits from which all other citrus types developed through natural hybrid speciation or artificial hybridization. Though citron cultivars take on a wide variety of physical forms, they are all closely related genetically. It is used in Asian and Mediterranean cuisine, traditional medicines, perfume, and religious rituals and offerings. Hybrids of citrons with other citrus are commercially more prominent, most notably lemons and many limes, which were created using citrons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg/330px-Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron","wikidata":"Q150064"},{"title":"Gobioidei","blocks":[{"text":"The Gobioidei are a suborder of percomorph fish. Many of these fishes are called gobies. It is by far the largest and most diverse order within the order Gobiiformes, and one of the most diverse groups of ray-finned fish in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Cryptocentrus_cinctus.JPG/330px-Cryptocentrus_cinctus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobioidei","wikidata":"Q901409"},{"title":"Citron (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Citron is a dark lemon color similar to that of the fruit citron. As a tertiary color on the RYB color wheel, it is an equal mix of orange and green pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Citron.jpg/330px-Citron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron_(color)","wikidata":"Q2974481"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ancient mosaic of Tiberian Synagogue depicting citrons","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASegment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg/500px-A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/A_species_of_citrus_